1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:03,190
Hi!

2
00:00:03,240 --> 00:00:05,271
I built AI Company Health.

3
00:00:05,321 --> 00:00:07,432
It's an agentic AI project:

4
00:00:07,482 --> 00:00:13,035
a simulated health insurer where every single employee is an AI agent.

5
00:00:13,085 --> 00:00:16,317
Fifty of them, across twelve departments,

6
00:00:16,367 --> 00:00:21,120
competing for customers in a town of a hundred AI residents.

7
00:00:23,060 --> 00:00:25,019
This is the town, Wattle Grove.

8
00:00:25,069 --> 00:00:26,640
Every resident has a job,

9
00:00:26,690 --> 00:00:27,937
an income, a family,

10
00:00:27,987 --> 00:00:29,299
and their own memory.

11
00:00:29,349 --> 00:00:31,373
Health cover is compulsory here,

12
00:00:31,423 --> 00:00:33,254
so each of them picks a fund,

13
00:00:33,304 --> 00:00:34,939
one of nine rivals, or us.

14
00:00:37,360 --> 00:00:40,210
Click on anyone, and you see their whole life.

15
00:00:40,260 --> 00:00:43,300
Where they work, which fund they're with and why,

16
00:00:43,350 --> 00:00:45,507
every claim and every conversation.

17
00:00:45,557 --> 00:00:48,596
And nothing in the company's numbers is scripted.

18
00:00:48,646 --> 00:00:51,749
Every sale and every claim comes from a decision a

19
00:00:51,799 --> 00:00:53,200
resident actually made.

20
00:00:54,660 --> 00:00:56,150
This is head office.

21
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:57,844
Each agent has a role,

22
00:00:57,894 --> 00:01:03,312
its own tools that query the company's live data, and long-term memory.

23
00:01:03,362 --> 00:01:05,700
This is Leo, our head of sales.

24
00:01:06,759 --> 00:01:09,487
I track token usage for every agent,

25
00:01:09,537 --> 00:01:12,728
day by day, so I can see exactly what each

26
00:01:12,778 --> 00:01:14,039
one costs to run.

27
00:01:14,989 --> 00:01:16,989
And I can just talk to him.

28
00:01:33,917 --> 00:01:38,446
Before answering, he checked the real numbers with his own tools.

29
00:01:38,496 --> 00:01:41,757
And he'll remember this conversation next time.

30
00:01:43,937 --> 00:01:45,591
I can also call a meeting.

31
00:01:45,641 --> 00:01:48,737
Pick a room, who should be there, and an agenda.

32
00:02:02,495 --> 00:02:04,349
They walk up to the boardroom,

33
00:02:04,399 --> 00:02:07,015
each one builds a deck from the live data,

34
00:02:07,065 --> 00:02:08,284
and they present it,

35
00:02:08,334 --> 00:02:09,935
right there on the screen.

36
00:02:09,985 --> 00:02:12,855
Then the minutes get written up automatically.

37
00:02:30,904 --> 00:02:33,022
So, what has it actually achieved?

38
00:02:33,072 --> 00:02:35,063
Over thirty-five simulated days,

39
00:02:35,113 --> 00:02:39,717
policies in force went from twenty to forty-six, with zero cancellations.

40
00:02:39,767 --> 00:02:42,459
That's made us the number one fund in town,

41
00:02:42,509 --> 00:02:45,264
with about forty-five percent of the market.

42
00:02:48,004 --> 00:02:50,724
Customer satisfaction is sitting at a hundred,

43
00:02:50,774 --> 00:02:52,831
every claim met its service target,

44
00:02:52,881 --> 00:02:56,564
and the business is running at around a twenty percent margin.

45
00:02:58,805 --> 00:03:02,328
The agents have also produced over thirty documents on their own.

46
00:03:02,378 --> 00:03:04,912
Decks, dashboards, reports and meeting minutes.

47
00:03:04,962 --> 00:03:08,101
And every number in them is fact-checked against the data,

48
00:03:08,151 --> 00:03:10,080
so if an agent gets something wrong,

49
00:03:10,130 --> 00:03:12,444
it's flagged, and the agent learns from it.

50
00:03:14,894 --> 00:03:17,757
Under the hood, every model call is tracked.

51
00:03:17,807 --> 00:03:21,266
So far, that's over five thousand calls and more than

52
00:03:21,316 --> 00:03:22,656
fifty million tokens.

53
00:03:22,706 --> 00:03:24,245
And every run is traced,

54
00:03:24,295 --> 00:03:27,357
so I can see exactly which tools an agent used,

55
00:03:27,407 --> 00:03:28,615
and what came back.

56
00:03:30,425 --> 00:03:33,858
Every Monday, the CEO agent reviews last week's goals and

57
00:03:33,908 --> 00:03:34,714
sets new ones.

58
00:03:34,764 --> 00:03:38,320
And an evaluation suite checks that agents answer with real

59
00:03:38,370 --> 00:03:39,603
numbers, not guesses.

60
00:03:39,653 --> 00:03:41,865
Right now, they pass five out of six.

61
00:03:43,254 --> 00:03:46,557
It's built with Google's Agent Development Kit,

62
00:03:46,607 --> 00:03:49,980
Vertex AI, A2A for agent-to-agent communication,

63
00:03:50,030 --> 00:03:51,977
LangGraph for the workflows,

64
00:03:52,027 --> 00:03:54,189
and a 3D front end in Three.js,

65
00:03:54,239 --> 00:03:56,186
all running on Google Cloud.

66
00:03:56,236 --> 00:03:57,612
Thanks for watching.

67
00:03:57,662 --> 00:03:59,894
I'd love to hear what you think!
